From 623e66582fdefd9a9139619b6f7ad010fb108af2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Filip=20Lewi=C5=84ski?= <filip.lewinski@3mdeb.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:23:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] soc/intel/common/block/gpio: keep locking pads outside of SMM
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

gpio_lock_pad() sent every caller outside of SMM to gpio_lock_pads()
once SOC_INTEL_COMMON_BLOCK_SMM_LOCK_GPIO_PADS was selected. That
includes gpio_configure_pad(), which locks the pads marked with a
PAD_CFG_*_LOCK macro in the mainboard pad tables while ramstage
configures them. gpio_lock_pads() only works in SMM, so it bailed out
with 'must be called from SMM!' and those pads were left unlocked.

Send every caller outside of SMM to gpio_non_smm_lock_pad(), whether or
not SMM locking is enabled, so that a board can lock pads from its pad
tables and from SMM finalize at the same time. Callers in SMM still go
through gpio_lock_pads().

Nothing selects SOC_INTEL_COMMON_BLOCK_SMM_LOCK_GPIO_PADS yet, so this
changes nothing on its own. Without it, enabling SMM pad locking on
Alder Lake would stop the PAD_CFG_*_LOCK entries in the pad tables of
boards such as google/brya and google/brox from being locked.

Change-Id: Iec16df3160c34dc96b037f89d660134f3ec4e0fb
Signed-off-by: Filip Lewiński <filip.lewinski@3mdeb.com>
Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/c/coreboot/+/95511
Reviewed-by: Angel Pons <th3fanbus@gmail.com>
Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) <no-reply@coreboot.org>
Reviewed-by: Nicholas Chin <nic.c3.14@gmail.com>
Origin: https://review.coreboot.org/c/coreboot/+/95511
Upstream-Status: Merged (2026-10-01)
Heads-Note: carried against coreboot-dasharo_nv4x 281a7fec1a1e; applies unmodified to the pinned fork.

---
 src/soc/intel/common/block/gpio/gpio.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/common/block/gpio/gpio.c b/src/soc/intel/common/block/gpio/gpio.c
index abd6695..933261c 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/common/block/gpio/gpio.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/common/block/gpio/gpio.c
@@ -721,7 +721,12 @@ int gpio_lock_pad(const gpio_t pad, enum gpio_lock_action lock_action)
 		.lock_action = lock_action
 	};
 
-	if (!ENV_SMM && !CONFIG(SOC_INTEL_COMMON_BLOCK_SMM_LOCK_GPIO_PADS))
+	/*
+	 * gpio_lock_pads() only works in SMM. Pads locked while configuring
+	 * them, i.e. from the pad tables in ramstage, have to go through the
+	 * non-SMM path even when the SoC also locks pads from SMM.
+	 */
+	if (!ENV_SMM)
 		return gpio_non_smm_lock_pad(&pads);
 
 	return gpio_lock_pads(&pads, 1);
